Four changes. (1) The robot-model library (urdf) hands out std::shared_ptr since ROS Melodic, no longer boost::shared_ptr; its own type names work in both. (2) The simulator switches gravity off for the arms at start, but did so before the robot was fully in the world: the setting was lost, and a shoulder then pushed against the arm's full weight without reaching its target (0.42 rad short of the neutral pose). It now waits for the robot, then checks every arm link and repeats the step until it holds. (3) Inverse kinematics answered every request with 'no solution': the solver of the current KDL library refuses a result array that is not sized to the number of joints, which older versions did themselves. The array is sized now. (4) Inverse kinematics looked the frames up at the time stamped on the request. A caller outside the simulation stamps the real time of day while the simulation counts from zero; it now uses the newest known frames. (Change 4 was made before the real cause, 3, was found; it is kept because the mismatch of the two clocks is real, but it is not shown to be needed.)

